// DOM extension of the ARS (L755-22, R755-14, R755-14-1; FINISH
// transfer from the DOM group, D-73). Thin link norms: territorial
// attribution, applicability of R543-1..7, exclusion of paid ARS from
// the CAF health/social action fund resources. The metropolitan
// computation (02-06) is untouched and territorially unrestricted;
// these rules only link it for DOM cases.
//
// DEONTIC MAP (pinned text only):
// - L. 755-22 "est attribuée ... dans les collectivités" -
//   institutional attribution status ars_attribuee_dom over the six
//   L. 751-1 collectivities, no duty: no Bearer [REDACTED] deadline or
//   sanction. The award is not gated on the department-only R755-14
//   status (D76 split).
// - R. 755-14 "sont applicables ... dans les départements" -
//   department-only applicability status ars_r543_applicable_dom over
//   R543-1..7, on department residence with provenance; no deontic
//   position.
// - R. 755-14-1 "versées dans les départements ... n'entre pas en
//   compte" - department-only exclusion status
//   ars_exclue_ressources_fonds, a classification without a bearer,
//   not a prohibition: the fund resource computation is out of scope
//   (B-PFARS-DOM-FONDS). The source condition is actual payment
//   (versées) in a department, so each rule requires matching
//   ars_verse evidence for the due amount being excluded plus
//   department residence. Both payment tracks (base amount and
//   standalone differential) are excluded by two rules over one head.
// No evaluative predicates: both residence facts are evidenced case
// facts with provenance (channel 3), independent per world; metro
// grounds stay upstream.
//
// READINGS (adopted, flagged for review):
// - Q-PFARS-DOM-1: the articles name no resident; the allocataire
//   parent's residence anchors the case (collectivity and department
//   facts stated independently with provenance).
// - Q-PFARS-DOM-2 SUPERSEDED by the D76 return: "collectivités"
//   (L755-22 award) and "départements" (R755-14, R755-14-1) are two
//   source classes with two independent facts (residence_dom,
//   residence_departement_dom); the one-scope reading of 2026-10-07
//   is withdrawn.
// - Metro L543/R543/D543 rules carry no territorial premise and keep
//   firing for every case; the DOM grant presupposes that regime.
//   R755-14's list is expressed as ONE applicability status: the
//   regulatory core functions as a block, and per-article heads would
//   stand unread. L543, D543 and R543-8/9 need no separate DOM norm:
//   their metro rules are territorially unrestricted.
// - In a collectivity-only world (no department residence) the award
//   holds where its premises hold; which R543 provisions govern there
//   is caller case input, this package concludes nothing for it
//   (B-PFARS-DOM-HORS-DEPT).
// - R755-14-1 speaks of the SUM of paid allowances. The package does
//   not calculate the fund's aggregate resources; each actually paid
//   track is excluded per child as a package coverage boundary
//   (B-PFARS-DOM-FONDS). No engine capability limitation is claimed.
//   CDC-routed payments are covered where they are actual payments:
//   routing is separate from the due amount, and ars_verse is the
//   execution fact for both channels.
//
// EDITIONS. All three versions cover the program window fully
// (L755-22 from 2015-10-16, R755-14 and R755-14-1 from 1990-06-29; no
// future versions); no predecessors pinned. Rules are effective
// [@2021-01-01, infinity). GENERATED_OUTPUT_PENDING: 01-sources.law,
// sources/css/L755-22.txt, R755-14.txt, R755-14-1.txt,
// sources/editions/*.txt, articles.json and fragment-map.json await
// tools/build_sources.py --write; @source/use-self resync is deferred
// to that run (new editions CSS_ED1990_06, CSS_ED2015_10; no renames).

